(BASE/'blind/instructions.md').write_text('''# Separate blind marking

Read `../candidate.goal.json`, `../task-and-marking.md`, the actual stimulus in `../stimulus/`, `scripts.json`, and every actual drawing referenced by a script. Do not read `../author/`, authoring source/expected scores, V1 marker outputs, the other marker's output or any reconciliation. Neutral case/drawing IDs contain no intended judgement. View the pixels. The ruler defines scale independently of screen zoom.

Mark all 20 fully written bilingual submissions independently, with A–D points, total and pass/fail separately for DE and EN, citing decisive evidence. The two languages are equivalent versions of one synthetic submission. Do not infer absent reasoning from drawings or correct values. Distinguish an omitted core from supplementary evidence, isolated slips from misconceptions, an omitted head with and without independent direction evidence, and consistent consequences of an already charged error.

Decide whether this own task is correct, age appropriate, clear, assessable in coach chat with an actual drawing, and sufficient for its single covered goal. Check the actual task stimulus rather than relying on solution prose. Check all four weights against the pass mark, including submissions with only the supplementary evidence of each criterion. Verify that a correct drawing/length without tip explanation cannot pass. Check whether the actual cases are consistent and whether the rubric yields reproducible bilingual scores. Report ambiguity by exact case and a minimal repair. Do not edit the candidate or communicate marks to the other reviewer. No positive verdict is assumed. These markings are content-quality evidence, never learner results.
''')

